# /etc/caps — capabilities held by an account that is not uid 0.
#
# Format: name:CAP_A,CAP_B
#
# uid 0 already holds every capability, so listing root here does nothing. The
# interesting use is to give one account one power without making it root: a
# backup account with CAP_DAC_READ_SEARCH can read anything and can change
# nothing, which is exactly what a backup needs.
#
# Examples (keep them commented out unless you want them):
#   backup:CAP_DAC_READ_SEARCH
#   auditor:CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE
